<section class="band band--night" id="therapists">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>The four ways Reem works with therapists</h2>
    <p class="intro-wide">Supervision, consultation, ethics hours and retreats are different
    things, and most therapists arrive wanting one of them in particular. Everything is online
    statewide, except where being outdoors is the point.</p>
    <div class="pathways">
      <a href="/for-therapists/lpc-supervision/">
        <h3>LPC supervision</h3>
        <p>Your 3,000 hours, supervised online anywhere in Texas. Four hours a month,
          trauma-informed, with EMDR consultation included while you are here. If you are an
          associate working toward licensure, start here.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/for-therapists/emdr-consultation/">
        <h3>EMDR consultation</h3>
        <p>Hours toward certification with an EMDRIA Approved Consultant. Online, focused on
        IFS-informed EMDR for phases one and two.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/for-therapists/ethics-ceus/">
        <h3>Ethics CEUs</h3>
        <p>The six ethics hours Texas asks for each renewal period, on secondary trauma. One
        online, or two in person on a trail walk among horses.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/for-therapists/retreats-training/">
        <h3>Retreats and training</h3>
        <p>Mindful trail retreats and equine-assisted training for Texas therapists. For when
        the growth edge is yours rather than a client's.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="intro-wide">Most therapists assemble these from four providers who have never met.
    Here they are one relationship: the EMDR consultation is free while you are supervised, the
    ethics hours count toward the half that needs an approved provider, and the same clinical
    lens runs through all of it.
    <a href="/for-therapists/">See how supervision, consultation, CEUs and retreats fit
    together</a>, with fees and formats side by side.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--sand" id="clients">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>Four ways Reem works with clients</h2>
    <p class="intro-wide">Reem sees a small number of adults and young adults for
    developmental trauma, C-PTSD, anxiety, panic and depression. When her schedule is full, the
    practice's <a href="/therapy/associates/">LPC Associates</a> have openings, including at
    sliding-scale fees.</p>
    <div class="pathways">
      <a href="/approach/ifs-informed-emdr/">
        <h3>IFS-informed EMDR</h3>
        <p>Internal agreement from the protective parts first, then processing.</p>
        <p class="card-who"><strong>Helps when</strong> EMDR has been tried before and stalled,
        or part of you wants this and part of you really does not.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/somatic-experiencing/">
        <h3>Somatic Experiencing</h3>
        <p>The pace your nervous system can actually hold, built rather than tested.</p>
        <p class="card-who"><strong>Helps when</strong> anxiety lives in your chest and stomach
        more than in your thoughts, or talking about it has stopped helping.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/approach/narm/">
        <h3>NARM</h3>
        <p>The pattern underneath, and where it was learned.</p>
        <p class="card-who"><strong>Helps when</strong> the trouble is a lifelong pattern rather
        than one event, and understanding your history has not changed it.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/therapy/equine/">
        <h3>Equine-assisted therapy</h3>
        <p>What the body does around a horse that notices everything.</p>
        <p class="card-who"><strong>Helps when</strong> you talk more easily with something else
        going on, or you are working on boundaries. Adults only.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="intro-wide">These four interlock rather than alternate, and the room is optional:
    <a href="/therapy/walk-and-talk/">walk and talk therapy</a> happens on a trail in central
    Texas, and equine sessions run with the horses near Dripping Springs.
    <a href="/therapy/">Learn more about therapy at Finding Balance</a>, including fees,
    formats, who each path suits and what a first session looks like.</p>
  </div>
</section>

